  "body": "Found by the in-house qualification run of 2026-10-18 on the AX7101 (dev e9cbb676, processor 2cbed0a9).\n\n**Behaviour.**\n- SET_CONTROL on the IDENTIFY CONTROL 0 sets value 255: SUCCESS, the notification is sent, and GET_CONTROL reads 255.\n- READ_DESCRIPTOR CONTROL 0 then still reports the current value 0 in value_details.\n\n**Required.**\n- IEEE 1722.1-2021 7.2.22 and 7.3.6.2: value_details carries the control's current value.\n- 6.2.2.8 lists CONTROL current values among the descriptor fields that change at run time.\n- Milan v1.2 5.3.12: the IDENTIFY control has value 255 in identification mode.\n\n**Source.** The READ_DESCRIPTOR current-value overlay (`docs/architecture/06_aecp_engine.md:289-300`; `hdl/aecp/ucode/gen_ucode.py:186-194`, the E_RDESC arms) covers ENTITY, AUDIO_UNIT, CLOCK_DOMAIN and STREAM_INPUT/OUTPUT only, not CONTROL.\n\n**Done when:**\n- READ_DESCRIPTOR CONTROL returns the current value after every SET_CONTROL, as the other four overlaid types do (#82);\n- a suite case and a planted mutant cover it;\n- the processor's suites and the parent's consumer gates pass.\n",
